        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Roy Orbison\n- Products: Early Orbison, \"Pretty One\", \"Uptown\"\n- Companies: Monument Records\n- Places: Hendersonville, Tennessee\n- Topics: compilation albums\n\nFacts:\n- Roy Kelton Orbison was born on April 23, 1936, and died on December 6, 1988.\n- Roy Orbison was an American singer-songwriter known for his distinctive, impassioned voice, complex song structures, and dark emotional ballads.\n- Early Orbison was released in 1964 as an album recorded by Roy Orbison on the Monument Records label at Monument's studios in Hendersonville, Tennessee.\n- Early Orbison was essentially a compilation of songs from Roy Orbison's first two Monument albums.\n- Early Orbison is notable for including \"Pretty One,\" the B-side of Roy Orbison's second Monument single, \"Uptown\".",
